2. Updated: CustomExceptions.java
The DatabaseOperationException now includes a single-argument constructor to resolve your compilation error, allowing other services to throw it with just a message string. All other existing exceptions remain untouched to ensure compatibility across your project.
package com.fincore.JournalService.Exception;

import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ResponseStatus;

/**
 * Centralized custom exception definitions for the Journal Service.
 * Rule 1: Ensures specific HTTP status codes are mapped to business failures.
 */
public class CustomExceptions {

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
    public static class FileProcessingException extends RuntimeException {
        public FileProcessingException(String message, Throwable cause) { super(message, cause); }
        public FileProcessingException(String message) { super(message); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.GONE)
    public static class CacheExpiredException extends RuntimeException {
        public CacheExpiredException(String message) { super(message); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CONFLICT)
    public static class ConcurrencyLockException extends RuntimeException {
        public ConcurrencyLockException(String message) { super(message); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
    public static class DatabaseOperationException extends RuntimeException {
        // Rule 1: Added single-argument constructor to fix compilation errors in SequenceService
        public DatabaseOperationException(String message) { super(message); }
        public DatabaseOperationException(String message, Throwable cause) { super(message, cause); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE)
    public static class RedisOperationException extends RuntimeException {
        public RedisOperationException(String message, Throwable cause) { super(message, cause); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY)
    public static class DataMappingException extends RuntimeException {
        public DataMappingException(String message) { super(message); }
    }

    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
    public static class BatchProcessingException extends RuntimeException {
        public BatchProcessingException(String message, Throwable cause) { super(message, cause); }
    }
}

Summary of Changes
 * Notification Fix: Changed NotificationWriterService from MANDATORY to REQUIRES_NEW. This allows the background threads to create their own transaction to save notifications even if the main controller transaction is absent or closed.
 * Compilation Fix: Added public DatabaseOperationException(String message) in CustomExceptions. This permits the use of throw new CustomExceptions.DatabaseOperationException("message") without needing a second Throwable argument.
 * Production Rules:
   * Maintained descriptive logs but removed generic e.getMessage() calls in NotificationWriterService to avoid accidental PII logging.
   * Added comments explaining the "Why" behind the transaction changes (Rule 3).
